cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BaySpec in your research, please cite the software version
  used in your analysis using the metadata in this file.
type: software
title: 'BaySpec: Bayesian inference for high-energy astrophysical spectra'
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Jun
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5485-5042'
version: 0.4.5
date-released: '2026-10-11'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jyangch/bayspec'
url: 'https://bayspec.readthedocs.io/'
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  BaySpec is a Python library for Bayesian inference on high-energy
  astrophysical spectra. It supports MCMC and nested sampling, joint
  fitting of multiple spectra and models, OGIP FITS spectra and responses,
  time-dependent spectral models, and local, astromodels, and XSPEC model
  libraries.
keywords:
  - astrophysics
  - spectral fitting
  - Bayesian inference
  - X-ray astronomy
  - gamma-ray astronomy
